<title>POLAND: BRE issue for Commerzbank approved.</title>
<headline>BRE issue for Commerzbank approved.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish Securities Commission (KPW) on Thursday approved for public trade Bank Rozwoju Eksportu SA's (BRE) new issue of 4.5 million shares offered to Germany's Commerzbank, the KPW said in a statement.</p>
<p>Commerzbank's purchase of the shares will increase its stake in the Polish bank to 48.8 percent from the current 32.8 percent. The subscription for the shares has been set for September 11-12.</p>
<p>BRE plans to spend proceeds from the issue on modernisation, credit expansion and developing its investment banking activities.</p>
<p>BRE currently has 14,500,000 shares outstanding.</p>
